clueweb09-en0008-78-35714.0 About us Contact Home Immunohistochemistry Links Forum Antibody Stains Protocols Epigenetics Immunohistochemistry Protocols Menu Immunohistochemistry Histology Microscopy Immunology Immunology Protocols Diseases and Disorders Lipoma Lipoma Lipoma Histology Benign tumor of fat cells Most common soft tissue tumor of adults Common in mid-adulthood Arise in the extremities, trunk Can also rarely arise in muscle tissue Lipoma Gross Appearance Soft, well-defined, mobile masses Painless Lipoma Histology Encapsulated masses of mature adipocytes within subcutaneous tissue, but can also be poorly circumscribed uncommonly. Cells show no pleomorphism, and are mature, white fat cells. Different Types of Lipomas Conventional Lipoma Fibrolipoma Angiolipoma Spindle Cell Lipoma Myelolipoma Pleomorphic Lipoma Lipoma Genetics Rearrangements are common. Links Copyright © 2007 Immunohistochemistry Protocols: Information on Immunohistochemistry, Immunology, Histology, Pathology and Chemistry. | All rights reserved.
