clueweb09-enwp03-38-13720.0 Vanderbilt Trophy From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search The Vanderbilt Knockout Teams national bridge championship is held at the spring American Contract Bridge League (ACBL) North American Bridge Championship (NABC). The Vanderbilt is a knock-out team event. The event typically last 7 days with each day being a round consisting of two sessions of 32 boards. The event is open and seeded. Contents 1 History 2 Winners 3 Sources 4 External links [edit] History The premier event of the Spring North American Championships is the Vanderbilt Knockout Teams. The history of the prestigious contest stretches back to 1928 when the man who invented contract bridge, Harold S. Vanderbilt, put the trophy bearing his name into play. The winners list is a whoýýýs who of bridge, a parade of the titans of the game. The Vanderbilt Trophy for the Vanderbilt Knockout Teams was donated in 1928 by Harold
